      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the thorough tests and clean implementation!\n\nOne edge case with narrowing `LIST_ITEM_REGEX` to `\\s{0,3}` in PS2 while raising `indentThreshold` via `getListIndentThreshold(currentListItem.prefix.length)`:\n\nWhen `currentListItem` has `prefix.length \u003e\u003d 4` (e.g. a 2-space indented sub-bullet `\"  - \"` or `\"  * \"`, or a 2-digit numbered item `\"10. \"`), `indentThreshold` becomes `5`. If it is followed by a nested sub-bullet indented by 4 spaces (e.g. `\"    - Level 3 bullet\"`):\n1. `LIST_ITEM_REGEX` (`\\s{0,3}`) does not match `\"    - Level 3 bullet\"`.\n2. `isUntouchedCodeOrQuoteLine(line, 5)` returns `false` because `leadingSpaces` (`4`) `\u003c 5`.\n3. It falls through to lines 186-192 (`leadingSpaces \u003e 0`) and gets merged onto the end of the Level 2 bullet (`\"  - Level 2 bullet - Level 3 bullet\"`).\n\nIf you keep `\\s*` in `LIST_ITEM_REGEX` and instead guard `listMatch` with `leadingSpaces \u003c indentThreshold` (and remove the early `LIST_ITEM_REGEX` check from `isUntouchedCodeOrQuoteLine`), both the 4-space code block test (`\"    - diff line\"` after `\"- bullet:\"`, where `4 \u003e\u003d indentThreshold (4)`) and 3+ level nested lists work cleanly:\n\n```ts\n    const indentThreshold \u003d\n      currentListItem !\u003d\u003d null\n        ? getListIndentThreshold(currentListItem.prefix.length)\n        : INDENTATION_THRESHOLD;\n\n    const leadingSpaces \u003d getLeadingSpacesCount(line);\n    const listMatch \u003d\n      leadingSpaces \u003c indentThreshold\n        ? line.trimEnd().match(LIST_ITEM_REGEX)\n        : null;\n    if (listMatch) {\n      flushParagraph();\n      flushListItem();\n      currentListItem \u003d {\n        prefix: listMatch[1],\n        lines: [listMatch[2].trim()],\n        lastRawLine: line.trimEnd(),\n      };\n      previousWasEmpty \u003d false;\n      continue;\n    }\n```\n(And similarly check `getLeadingSpacesCount(line) \u003c prevIndentThreshold` before matching `LIST_ITEM_REGEX` in `detectFormattingErrors` around line 431.)",
