      "message": "Minor edge case: if a commit message without a `Change-Id` footer ends with a single-line 4-space indented code block containing `key: value` or `key\u003dvalue` (e.g. `Fix config\\n\\nExample:\\n\\n    timeout: 30s\\n`), `footer.length \u003d\u003d\u003d 1`, so `isListOrIndentedBlock` evaluates to `false`. `FOOTER_REGEX.test(line.trim())` then matches it as a footer, causing `detectFormattingErrors` to flag `LEADING_SPACES` and `formatCommitMessage` to strip the 4-space indentation.\n\nAdding `footer.every(line \u003d\u003e isUntouchedCodeOrQuoteLine(line))` to `isListOrIndentedBlock` prevents 4-space code blocks (and quotes/comments) at the end of a message from being misclassified as footers:\n\n```ts\n  const isListOrIndentedBlock \u003d\n    footer.some(\n      line \u003d\u003e\n        getLeadingSpacesCount(line) \u003c INDENTATION_THRESHOLD \u0026\u0026\n        LIST_ITEM_REGEX.test(line.trimEnd())\n    ) ||\n    footer.every(line \u003d\u003e isUntouchedCodeOrQuoteLine(line)) ||\n    (footer.length \u003e 1 \u0026\u0026\n      footer.every(line \u003d\u003e getLeadingSpacesCount(line) \u003e 0)) ||\n    (footer.length \u003e 1 \u0026\u0026\n      footer[0].trim().endsWith(\u0027:\u0027) \u0026\u0026\n      !FOOTER_REGEX.test(footer[0].trim()));\n```",
